module System

### The protocol for values that can make an independent duplicate of themselves with `duplicate`. A record that `=`
### copies obeys it whatever its member variables are: its `duplicate` is that copy (a handle member, such as a
### `Guarded`, is shared by it). An entity, or a value that holds one, is duplicated member by member, so it obeys
### Copyable only when every member does. `duplicate` is inserted wherever an independent duplicate is required (e.g.
### building a value into a collection).
protocol Copyable
needs Copyable everywhere
    ### Returns an independent duplicate of this value (a deep copy for an aggregate; the refcount-share
    ### `assign` for an Assignable managed leaf, which is independent since the buffer is immutable).
    ### :returns: A duplicate of this value with its own valid lifetime and invariants.
    @readonly
    routine Me.duplicate() -> Me
